  "emoji": "🙂",
  "summary": "Say how you feel: tired, happy, sad, worried, angry, hungry or thirsty, with the right form for a man or a woman.",
  "intro": "Layla and Sami visit Daniel at his flat with a pot of soup. Feelings are adjectives, so they agree with the person: أَنَا مُتْعَب (a man) but أَنَا مُتْعَبَة (a woman). Adjectives on the pattern faʿlān, like عَطْشَان (thirsty) and غَضْبَان (angry), make their feminine with -ā: عَطْشَى, غَضْبَى. To ask how someone feels, say كَيْفَ تَشْعُرُ؟ to a man and كَيْفَ تَشْعُرِينَ؟ to a woman.",
  "objectives": [
    "Name seven feelings: tired, happy, sad, worried, angry, hungry, thirsty",
    "Use the masculine and feminine forms correctly",
    "Ask كَيْفَ تَشْعُرُ؟ and كَيْفَ تَشْعُرِينَ؟ and answer them",
    "Say 'I feel bored' and 'I feel better'"
  ],
